			<div class="content" id="post-content-2696779">
									

<p>I don't really understand the criticism (which you are not the first to provide) that it's 'shoehorned' in there. By attributing this to Gamers Against Weed, it succinctly contextualizes the backstory as &quot;pranksters turned political&quot;, rather than &quot;activists with a sense of humor&quot; which might be implied otherwise. Now, 'activists with a sense of humor' is <em>okay</em>, but it's not a story.</p>
<p>This was conceived from the start as one of the anomalous items used during protests mentioned by <a href="/scp-2293">SCP-2293</a> &#8212; I asked myself 'How would GAW help out in their own way?' and went from there. It's not &quot;necessary&quot;, but I know from experience how easy it is to keep trimming parts that aren't &quot;necessary&quot; until the piece is bare-bones and the readers all get this sense that there should be something more to it. For the amount of flavor it gives to the piece, I think GAW is absolutely worth the sentence it takes to set up.</p>

